# Files an update must never overwrite, because the machine owns them
# rather than the repository.
#
# custom/ is the documented place for a user's own Hyprland settings: the
# installer writes each file once and never again, and Settings keeps the
# keyboard-layouts block in custom/general.lua. The shipped copies are
# stubs, so without this every update would offer to replace a user's file
# with an empty one and, running unattended, would take that offer.
.config/hypr/custom/

# Settings > Display rewrites monitors.lua with explicit monitor blocks the
# first time anything changes; the shipped copy is the auto-scale heuristic
# that runs until then. Replacing it would throw every tuned resolution,
# refresh rate, scale, position and VRR choice back to guesswork.
.config/hypr/monitors.lua
